WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.210
AJA HAMMERLY: In
this Cloud Minute,

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:03.584
I'll show you how to export
logs from Stackdriver Logging

00:00:03.584 --> 00:00:05.947
into Cloud Storage,
BigQuery, or Pub/Sub.

00:00:05.947 --> 00:00:08.280
Exporting logs to cloud storage
allows you to store them

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.140
for extended periods of time.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.990
Exporting to BigQuery allows you
to do more complicated analysis

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:14.087
of your logs.

00:00:14.087 --> 00:00:16.170
And exporting Pub/Sub
allows you to send your logs

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:18.390
to other applications.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:23.010
From the Stackdriver logs
viewer, click on Create Export.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.260
You can limit your export
by using the logging filters

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.690
if you need to.

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:29.467
Now you need to name your sync.

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:31.675
You can use alphanumeric
characters, underscore dash,

00:00:31.675 --> 00:00:34.460
and period.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.092
Now it's time to
select a service.

00:00:36.092 --> 00:00:37.550
If you choose Cloud
Storage, you'll

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.320
be asked to pick
a storage bucket.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:43.900
If you choose BigQuery, you'll
be asked to choose a data set.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.700
Now click Create Sync.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:49.032
Logs exported to BigQuery will
show up almost immediately.

00:00:49.032 --> 00:00:51.490
Logs exported to Cloud Storage
are batched and will show up

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:52.780
approximately once an hour.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.300
Now I can use the
power of BigQuery

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.690
to look deeper into my logs.

